## About <a name = "about"></a>
Accela is a Discord bot for searching AniList. Use slash commands to find
anime and manga, then browse the results in Discord.

Currently in development.

## How it works <a name = "working"></a>

Accela uses AniList wrappers to build queries and fetch the requests through the AniList API. Requests are displayed in embeds with a page system allowing multiple results.

Accela is currently under development in Node.JS V24.19.0

## Usage <a name = "usage"></a>

To use Accela, use one of the slash commands such as:
```
/anime [Anime]
```
> All commands in Accela are slash commands and no chat commands are included. Several commands have optional or mandatory parameters that can be used to refine the search.

Accela will then display an embed with all information made in the request it found on the anime with 4 additional choices in a selectable menu.

### Example:

```
/anime name:Kino no Tabi format:OVA status:Finished
```

## Getting Started <a name = "getting_started"></a>
These instructions will get you a copy of the project up and running on your local machine for development and testing purposes. See [deployment](#deployment) for notes on how to deploy the project on a live system.

### Prerequisites

What things you need to install the software and how to install them.

- Node.js 22 or newer and npm.
- A Discord application and bot 

### Installing

1. Clone the repository and install dependencies:

   ```sh
   git clone https://github.com/Klarp/Accela.git
   cd Accela
   npm install
   ```

2. Create a `.env` file in the project root:

   ```env
   DISCORD_TOKEN=your_bot_token
   CLIENT_ID=your_application_id
   GUILD_ID=your_server_id
   ```

   `GUILD_ID` is only required when deploying commands to one server.

   **Keep your bot token private.** Never commit your `.env` file or share
   your token. If it is exposed, reset it in the Discord Developer Portal.

3. Add the bot to your server through the Developer Portal using the
   `bot` and `applications.commands` scopes.

4. Deploy the slash commands using one of the methods below, then start
   the bot:

   ```sh
   npm start
   ```

## Deploying slash commands <a name="deployment"></a>

Deploy commands to a single server for development:

```sh
node src/guild_deploy.js
```

Or deploy them globally:

```sh
node src/global_deploy.js
```

Run the appropriate deployment command again whenever you change a slash
command's name, description, or options. Global command updates may take
some time to appear.


